# ⚠️ Critical file, identified as fix #2 in 01-pilotage/DECISIONS.md § 4 bis.
#
# Without it, the `COPY . .` of the multi-stage Dockerfiles ships `node_modules` and the Nx
# cache to the Docker daemon: several hundred megabytes of build context, for 3
# applications x 3 environments, on every Jenkins build.

# Dependencies and caches - rebuilt inside the build stage
node_modules
**/node_modules
.nx
**/.next
tmp
out-tsc
coverage
reports
test-results

# Build output, at any depth. `dist` alone would only match the root one, and a local
# `nx prune` leaves apps/api/dist/workspace_modules behind — which the build stage then
# copies in, giving Nx two projects called @theetiptop-contest/shared and failing the build.
dist
**/dist

# Generated Prisma client: produced inside the build stage by `prisma generate`.
apps/api/src/generated

# Secrets - injected at runtime by Jenkins, never in an image layer
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Git history - useless at runtime, and carries the whole past of the repository
.git
.gitignore
.github

# Local tooling
.vscode
.idea
.claude
.editorconfig
.prettierrc
.prettierignore
**/*.log

# Docs and tests - no reason to weigh down a production image
**/*.md
!README.md
e2e
**/*.spec.ts
**/*.test.ts
playwright-report
test-results

# System files
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
